7.1 Each Party represents and warrants that it has the power and authority to enter into and perform this Agreement.

7.2 NEITHER PARTY SHALL BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR ANY LOSS OF PROFITS, REVENUES, DATA, USE OR GOODWILL, WHETHER INCURRED DIRECTLY OR INDIRECTLY.

7.3 THE AGGREGATE LIABILITY OF EACH PARTY UNDER THIS AGREEMENT SHALL NOT EXCEED THE AMOUNTS PAID OR PAYABLE UNDER THIS AGREEMENT IN THE TWELVE (12) MONTHS PRECEDING THE EVENT GIVING RISE TO THE CLAIM.


8. DISPUTE RESOLUTION AND GOVERNING LAW

8.1 This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of {{ governing_law | default("Sri Lanka") }}.

8.2 Either Party may seek injunctive or other equitable relief to protect its intellectual property or confidential information in any court of competent jurisdiction.

8.3 Any other dispute arising out of or in connection with this Agreement shall be resolved by {{ dispute_resolution | default("Arbitration") }} administered in accordance with the chosen institution's rules, and the decision shall be final and binding on the Parties.


9. GENERAL PROVISIONS

9.1 This Agreement constitutes the entire agreement between the Parties and supersedes all prior understandings, whether written or oral.

9.2 No amendment or waiver of any provision of this Agreement shall be binding unless in writing and signed by both Parties.

9.3 Nothing in this Agreement shall be construed to create a partnership, joint venture, agency, or employment relationship between the Parties.

9.4 This Agreement may be executed in counterparts, each of which shall be deemed an original.

9.5 Force Majeure: neither Party shall be liable for failure to perform its obligations to the extent caused by events outside its reasonable control.

